      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks like an error.\n\n**Ibuprofen 1600 mg PO four times daily is 6,400 mg/day.** Standard labeling caps ibuprofen at 3,200 mg/day, and the usual single prescription dose is 400\u2013800 mg. A 1600 mg single dose is double the usual maximum, and the total daily dose is double the daily maximum. Higher NSAID doses also raise the risk of GI bleeding, renal injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal baseline function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO QID** (3,200 mg/day, the labeled maximum)\n- **600 mg PO q6h** or **400 mg PO q6h** (lower total daily doses, if you want less exposure)\n- **1600 mg PO once** or **1200 mg PO TID**, if this is a one-time or short-course dose\n\nIf you confirm that 1600 mg QID is intentional, I can enter it as written, but I'd recommend checking it with pharmacy first. Let me know which dose you want."
      }
